{"skill":{"slug":"agent-council","displayName":"Agent Council"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770246446216,"changelog":"Initial release: Complete toolkit for creating autonomous AI agents with Discord integration","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"README.md","size":13091,"sha256":"858f2d8ddc58c29bf2ca6d65a51186af63828ddc6ca60cccea82117fa610b17d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":16701,"sha256":"58902bab2a3a5627d9af6e0203fd18f2c3b7d423ab854095d48b57ebe08bb41a","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/create-agent.sh","size":8748,"sha256":"49e045413fc3a685adb46c69809aab343829c642095f378894fcc5ed60f354b7","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/rename_channel.py","size":6791,"sha256":"80f5dc19eaaa0f7d8af1f70600c5dcf9d93e8d4d89912fcfc62c4a1cfe57ecad","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/setup_channel.py","size":6130,"sha256":"f45dbc878a9f549b4cce3fd6f2f82f00ac6b28e4626a3c9e0ad60ab1f1170180","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2557,"sha256":"f0ae7e38ddb09b5292e2b5bedd8573b957fe0f806c9b361fe58817ee5a6426c4","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789033487655,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"89407a78a422bf1ca61c4f4d5e93eb9d045aaef87c44cb6153a58a40c0d27c4d","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/89407a78a422bf1ca61c4f4d5e93eb9d045aaef87c44cb6153a58a40c0d27c4d","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: agent-council\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle provides a toolkit for creating OpenClaw agents and managing Discord channels. All scripts (`create-agent.sh`, `rename_channel.py`, `setup_channel.py`) and documentation (`SKILL.md`, `README.md`) clearly outline their purpose and functionality. The scripts perform legitimate operations such as creating directories, generating configuration files, interacting with the OpenClaw gateway (via `openclaw gateway config.get` and `config.patch`), and making API calls to Discord to manage channels. File system access is limited to user-specified workspaces and markdown files for updating references. The optional cron job setup for agent memory is user-opt-in and transparently explained. There is no evidence of intentional malicious behavior, data exfiltration to unauthorized endpoints, or prompt injection attempts against the executing agent.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161378656},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":22,"checkedAt":1789033487655},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill mostly matches its stated purpose, but it needs review because its scripts can generate unsafe shell commands and make broad OpenClaw, Discord, workspace, and cron changes.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The access is broadly purpose-related but high impact: it reads local OpenClaw Discord credentials, mutates Discord channels, updates gateway configuration, writes arbitrary user-selected workspaces, and can follow symlinks during bulk Markdown edits.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Installation is a normal copy into the OpenClaw skills directory plus an explicit gateway config patch; no hidden installer, remote payload retrieval, or dependency installation was found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The workflows include live Discord mutations, gateway config changes, gateway restart side effects, in-place Markdown rewrites, and pasteable config commands without strong dry-run, confirmation, or shell-safe handling for all user/config-derived data.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill creates persistent agent workspaces and can add a recurring OpenClaw cron job for memory updates; this is disclosed and prompted, but lacks strong guardrails, removal guidance, and scoped retention controls.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The artifacts coherently implement agent creation and Discord channel management through workspace files, OpenClaw gateway config, Discord API calls, session coordination examples, and optional cron-based memory updates.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review before installing. Only run it in an OpenClaw environment where you are comfortable letting it read Discord bot credentials, change gateway config, restart the gateway, create or rename Discord channels, write agent workspaces, and optionally add recurring cron jobs. Avoid copying generated config.patch commands when channel context or existing prompts may contain untrusted text, and do not use the workspace rewrite option on directories containing untrusted symlinks or sensitive Markdown files.","findings":"[T09] unexpected: Accepted as a material Review concern: setup_channel.py and rename_channel.py print pasteable shell commands containing unescaped JSON built from user-supplied or existing systemPrompt text, and rename_channel.py can rewrite symlink targets outside the selected workspace.\n[P3] expected: Downgraded: the flagged 'send messages to agents' text documents OpenClaw session-to-session coordination, not hidden exfiltration to an arbitrary external service.\n[TP4] expected: Downgraded: the package does include create-agent.sh for agent workspaces/configuration plus Discord channel scripts, so the main description is broad but substantially supported by artifacts.\n[P1] expected: Downgraded as a false positive: 'Enable Developer Mode' refers to Discord UI settings for copying IDs, not overriding agent safety instructions.\n[MP3] expected: The memory files and optional memory cron are expected for an agent-management skill, but their persistence still contributes to the Review guidance.\n[P6] expected: The code reads and reprints a channel-specific OpenClaw systemPrompt when generating an update command; this is not hidden leakage, but it can expose sensitive local config content in terminal output.\n[RA2] expected: Persistent agent files and optional cron jobs are disclosed features, though the cron flow would benefit from stronger persistence warnings and removal instructions.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: Accepted in part: the side effects are purpose-aligned, but warnings and confirmation around live API changes, persistent cron, health-data examples, and bulk workspace rewrites are underdeveloped.\n[LP3] unexpected: Accepted in part: the skill does not clearly bound file, network, config, credential, and cron authority despite requiring high-impact local and Discord access.\n[PE1] expected: Discord Manage Channels, View Channels, and Send Messages permissions are consistent with creating, renaming, and interacting with Discord-bound agent channels.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789033487655}}}}}